# Publication hygiene: user-supplied game content, vendor binaries and Sony-owned art never enter the repo
#
# patches/ needs two rules, not one. Bloodborne.xml directly under it is the port's built-in
# patch database (scripts/patches.py defaults --xml to it and refuses to start without it),
# and its patch lists carry local corrections on top of shadps4-emu/ps4_cheats, so it must be
# tracked. The GoldHEN/ and shadPS4/ subdirectories are unmodified third-party collections and
# stay out. Matching "/patches/*/" rather than "/patches/" keeps both facts in one place.
/patches/*/
/dumps/
/savedata/
/sys_modules/
/mods/
/dlss/
/nvngx*.dll
/patches-stamp.json
/logo/bg2.jpg